Arcana, The Seven Archives of FreeBSD: an agent for every FreeBSD host
and a web console for the fleet.  The console, a progressive web app
logged in to with a security key or a passkey (WebAuthn), shows each
host's jails, rc.d services, packages, network tables and resource
usage, and changes them: jails are started and stopped, addresses
changed live or in jail.conf, services driven and configured, packages
upgraded on hosts and in jails.  Changes run as jobs on the host, which
finish even when the console is cut off, and each comes with its
workflow as a graph: the library calls, system calls and programs it
used, with the programs' output.

Each host runs arcana-agent(8), the only privileged part, served over
cblink with mutual TLS; arcana-enrol(8) joins a host to the console with
a one-time token.  The console, arcana-console(8), serves on libwebsockets
and runs unprivileged.  arcanactl(8) talks to an agent from a shell, and
jailconf(8) changes one value in jail.conf in place, like sysrc(8) does
for rc.conf.

Without the CONSOLE option only the host's programs are built.
